<title>FINLAND: EMU UNDECIDED BIGGEST GROUP IN FINNISH PARLIAMENT.</title>
<headline>EMU UNDECIDED BIGGEST GROUP IN FINNISH PARLIAMENT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fifty-five members of parliament are for joining Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) while 44 are against, but the biggest group in parliament are the 60 undecided, daily Iltalehti reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The paper surveyed the legislature and was unable to reach 14 of the 200 MPs.</p>
<p>Twelve did not give their view and 14 hesitated, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
</text>
